# agent-workspace:v8:start
# Python bytecode cache (any directory, not just the hook runtime -- this
# framework's own repo ships real Python source under lib/, and running any
# python3 command against it generates __pycache__/*.pyc that must never be
# committed).
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Agent workspace local state
.agents/state/
CLAUDE.local.md

# Claude Code's own ephemeral worktree-isolation directories for background
# agents (each is a real, separate git working tree -- committing one nests
# a full second .git inside this repo).
.claude/worktrees/

# Optional generated indexes
graphify-out/cache/
# agent-workspace:v8:end

# --- project-specific exception, added deliberately, not by the framework ---
# This repo IS the Adaptive Engine's own showcase, so shared tier, identity,
# active-agent, and MCP opt-in state is committed instead of staying local-only.
# Machine/session-specific profile and task-policy files remain ignored. See
# docs/decision-matrix.md and CONTRIBUTING.md for the rationale.
# ownership.json and project-id are required by doctor_project(); excluding them made a
# fresh clone of this very repo fail `doctor --deep` -- caught by an independent
# review (docs/audits/2026-09-05-pre-publish-review.md, finding 3) that a
# committed working copy never surfaces since the file already exists on disk.
# Git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so the
# directory itself must be un-ignored first, then re-ignored file-by-file.
!.agents/state/
.agents/state/*
!.agents/state/tier.json
!.agents/state/tier.md
!.agents/state/tier-history.jsonl
!.agents/state/risk-answers.json
!.agents/state/active-agents.json
!.agents/state/ownership.json
!.agents/state/project-id
!.agents/state/mcp-enabled.json

# --- second project-specific exception, opposite direction from the one above ---
# docs/CURRENT_STATE.md is normally committed by the framework's own default
# (ratchery init installs it expecting a team to track it) -- this repo
# deliberately does NOT commit its own copy. It holds session-to-session
# development notes for whoever is actively working on this codebase, not
# something a downstream user or contributor needs to see. See CONTRIBUTING.md
# "This repo runs its own tooling on itself" for the rationale. The file still
# exists locally; `doctor` treats the exact ignore entry as a deliberate
# opt-out instead of warning in every clean clone. The audit linked below
# flagged the load-bearing references to check before doing this; verified none
# needed code changes, only this ignore + untrack.
docs/CURRENT_STATE.md

# Local release output; tagged releases are published by GitHub Actions.
dist/
